\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Watch: Dlr Weakness Could Nudge US To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Takeshi Takeuchi \par \uc2 867 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 1999\par 02:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Don't rule out the possibility of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen, some analysts in Tokyo said. \par \par \uc2  Even if, as expected, the Bank of Japan doesn't ease monetary policy soon - reportedly a key condition for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the U.S. Federal Reserve may still be spurred to action, they said. \par \par \uc2  The catalyst for dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to come from conditions in the U.S., not Japan, the analysts said. \par \par \uc2  In particular, the trade-weighted average of the dollar against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been falling steadily in the last three months. The indexed average is calculated daily by the U.S. Federal Reserve Board and serves as a benchmark in setting U.S. monetary and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  In June, while the BOJ was buying dollars in an effort to weaken the yen, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was firmly in a rising trend on a trade-weighted basis, so it's no surprise the Fed didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  then, the analysts noted. \par \par \uc2  But after hitting its year-peak of 98.03 on July 12, the index has been falling sharply. It dipped to 91.96 on Oct. 1, almost as low as a year earlier when the dollar's plunge in the wake of the collapse a major U.S. hedge fund threatened global markets. \par \par \uc2  "The current level of the dollar index is a bit serious. If the U.S. lets the index keep falling, concerns about a dollar free fall will likely surface," said Yukihiko Hashimoto, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Sanwa Bank. \par \par \uc2  "In that case, the U.S. Fed would have to step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stem the dollar's fall regardless of whether the BOJ further eases monetary policy," he said. \par \par \uc2  In the last week, dollar-yen trading has settled into a range roughly between Y104 and Y107.50. Wednesday afternoon in Tokyo, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted around Y107.35. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par             U.S. Stock, Bond Mkts May Be Key\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The calm blanketing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets in recent sessions combined with\par the dollar's ability to bounce off a 44-month low of Y103.20 hit on\par Sept. 15 has eased \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  concerns.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But if a further slide in the dollar threatens to undermine U.S. stock\par and bond prices, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could become an option.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "What appears to worry the U.S. most is the possibility of a\par simultaneous drop of the dollar, stock and bond prices, which would\par probably be a recipe that would crush the U.S. economy," said Shuji\par Takano, assistant manager of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at ABN AMRO Bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The repeated failure of the Dow Jones Industrial Average to hold above\par 10400 points is one signal that could point to a major consolidation,\par some analysts said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. officials agreed to include a yen-related statement in the\par communique released at a meeting of the Group of Seven in Washington\par last month partly because of fears about an abrupt and sharp slowdown of\par the U.S. economy, officials familiar with the meeting said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The statement said G-7 nations "shared Japan's concerns about the\par recent appreciation of the yen and its impact on the Japanese economy\par and the world economy."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "What the U.S. was worrying about was not the yen's rise against the\par dollar per se, but the possibility that the yen's rise could induce a\par sudden outflow of overseas capital from U.S. assets and choke off the\par U.S. economy," a senior government official close to the talks told Dow\par Jones Newswires on condition of anonymity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As for the BOJ, the chances are slim at best that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par will ease policy at the next meeting of its policy board Oct. 13,\par analysts said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's quarterly business sentiment survey "tankan,"\par released Monday, showed that the sentiment has improved for the third\par straight quarter, the first three-quarter string of improvements in\par almost five years.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par               Three Straight Tankan Improvements\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The third straight quarter of improvement in the tankan usually would\par give the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cause to shift to tightening mode. If the BOJ were\par to ease policy now, it would likely have a hard time coming up with an\par adequate explanation for the move," said Makoto Ishikawa, an economist\par at Japan Research Institute.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The BOJ is most likely to keep the current zero-interest rate policy\par unchanged," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If the BOJ doesn't change its policy, the dollar will likely resume\par its slide against the yen, possibly to near Y103, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers said.\par Overseas players who are accumulating dollars assuming the BOJ will ease\par would start dumping dollars for yen, they noted.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The BOJ would then highly likely \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the dollar,\par since its selling would be caused by its own policy decision," said\par Sanwa's Hashimoto. "But if the BOJ's solo action turns out to be\par ineffective, the U.S. may well follow suit because it can't let the\par adverse effects spill into stock and bond markets."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By Takeshi Takeuchi; 813-5255-2934; ttakeuchi@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 07-10-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0000GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1187 4256 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dva707ayn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
