\par\par \b \uc2  Fischer -3: BOJ Should Not Sterilize  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 1999\par 20:48\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Fischer said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sustained recovery is crucial for the same to occur in the rest of Asia. For that, he added the country must implement another supplemental fiscal stimulus budget this year and the Bank of Japan must aggressively seek an expansionary monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  Fischer said the current effective 0% level of Japanese interest rates need not constrain the Bank of Japan's expansionary agenda. \par \par \uc2  He also urged the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to target an expanded monetary base. \par \par \uc2  "With interest rates at zero, there is a question of what more the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can do. One answer is to continue to expand the money stock by injecting even more liquidity into the system." \par \par \uc2  He said the Bank of Japan should "be buying assets at the long end, the middle end, wherever they can" in the yield curve. By expanding its debt security assets in this way, the Bank of Japan could get around the constraints of a zero interest-rate environment," Fischer said. \par \par \uc2  He said money supply targeting would, in Japan's case, be more effective than inflation rate targeting. \par \par \uc2  Some economists have urged the BOJ to target a higher inflation rate as a means of inducing consumers to spend. But Fischer said while he supported inflation targeting in general, it wouldn't work in a country where inflation is nonexistent like Japan. \par \par \uc2  He also addressed suggestions that the BOJ not sterilize its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to weaken the yen. While he acknowledged that this was an alternative means of expanding liquidity in the banking system, Fischer said it shouldn't form the basis of the BOJ's money supply management policy. He argued that there would often be a mismatch between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  aims and its money supply objectives. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  10-07-99 \par \par \uc2  1448EDT \par \par \uc2  4213 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010826dva701jvt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
