\par\par \b \uc2  Unsterilised  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  moves 'unrealistic'- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  source. \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 1999\par 06:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON, Sept 27 (Reuters) - Leaving \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "unsterilised" as a way to supply extra liquidity is unrealistic under Japan's current policy framework, said a Japanese delegation source to the weekend G7 meeting on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be an option in only those countries that use \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy as monetary policy," said the source, who was accompanying Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa and Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami at the G7 and international conferences. \par \par \uc2  "Unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not just ineffective but can become a source of market confusion and volatility in Japan and all the other industrial nations that do not treat \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy as monetary policy," he said. \par \par \uc2  A number of economists and some politicians have demanded that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after its yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , leave the pool of yen in the market. \par \par \uc2  "The argument that Japan does not provide ample liquidity because the BOJ absorbs all the surpluses caused by yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is erroneous," the source said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ has been providing a money market surplus of a massive one trillion yen on a daily basis and the surplus is caused by \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and also other factors such as bank note issues and fiscal payments, he said. \par \par \uc2  "It is hardly possible for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to separate the surplus as a result of yen selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from all the other surpluses caused by bank notes and fiscal payments." \par \par \uc2  Also, economists calling for unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have to be aware that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  interevention does not take place every day on a regular basis and it can be a fund shortfall factor as well, he said. \par \par \uc2  If \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  engaged in unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  it would mean funds being drained from the market. \par \par \uc2  Unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only make the level of the daily surplus in the money market quite volatile, he said. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv9s02wf9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
