\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of Japan Voted 7-2 In August To Maintain Current Monetary Policy \b0\par\par\uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 1999\par 10:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The Bank of Japan's policy board decided by a 7-2 vote to maintain its current monetary policy at its Aug. 13 meeting, according to the minutes from the meeting released Monday. \par \par \uc2  Board members Eiko Shinotsuka and Nobuyuki Nakahara dissented, the minutes said. Nakahara proposed setting a target for the monetary base with the aim of giving rise to inflationary expectations. His proposal was voted down 8-2, the minutes said. \par \par \uc2  Shinotsuka proposed raising the target for the key unsecured overnight call rate - the rate banks charge each other for unsecured short-term loans - to around 0.25%. The Bank of Japan currently guides the rate down to effectively zero. Shinotsuka's proposal was voted down eight to one, according to the minutes. \par \par \uc2  Several members agreed that there would be little impact on financial markets even if the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted unsterilized yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "One member explained that unsterilized yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the zero interest rate policy simply meant that the supply of excessive funds would increase by the amount of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the day of the settlement. This member stated that such kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  could hardly be considered to have an effect," the minutes said. \par \par \uc2  The member also said that unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only have an effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if interest rates fell. Since there's likely to be little impact as interest rates are already near zero, such action wouldn't affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the member argued. "Several members agreed with this opinion," the minutes said. \par \par \uc2  Several members said that even if there was a temporary reaction in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it wouldn't be long-lasting. \par \par \uc2  Several members "asserted that the Bank should not take measures that it did not consider to be effective theoretically, just to take advantage of the market's perception," the minutes said. "They continued that, even if such a measure had some effect in the short term, it would only be temporary." \par \par \uc2  Many members said that the yen's appreciation "was unlikely to have a significant impact on the economy," the minutes said. \par \par \uc2  They said that the rise in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was because of an improvement in the assessment of the economy. \par \par \uc2  The members also said that "so far, the extent of the rise had been limited and therefore was unlikely to affect firms' business plans," the minutes said. \par \par \uc2  In addition, the members said that a drop in stock prices and rise in long-term interest rates around the time of the board meeting "posed little downside risk to economic activity." \par \par \uc2  Some members said that the Bank of Japan should reconsider its practice of leaving one trillion yen ($9.60 billion) of excess banking reserves at almost all of its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But many members said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't simultaneously set targets for both interest rates and the quantity of money in markets. \par \par \uc2  They also said that there is no need for the Bank of Japan to announce a target for excess reserves, as one member had suggested the Bank of Japan do. \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 1999 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020329dv9r03r9l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
