\par\par \b \uc2  Yen strength undimmed with G7 action a faint hope. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 730 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 1999\par 14:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 27 (Reuters) - Prospects of a turnaround in the yen's relentless rise remained dim on Monday, with the tentative steps taken by Group of Seven financial superpowers to tame the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amounting to little so far. \par \par \uc2  Finance Ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs of the Group of Seven, in a rare reference to a specific \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said in a statement after their meeting on Saturday that they shared Japan's concern about the effect of a higher yen might have on Japan's and world economies. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the dollar could gain some support from the fact that yen strength was a major topic at the meeting, but added that this was no Plaza Accord, which in 1985 heralded a steep dollar depreciation fuelled by joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  For one thing, any joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  must be conducted with a decisive will to reverse the yen's uptrend - a tricky proposition given the U.S. trade deficit already running at record levels. \par \par \uc2  A "smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to merely slow down the yen's rise would be met with the same market indifference the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent months had faced. "If they were deliberately trying to drive dollar/yen higher, perhaps we can be confident of a floor ahead of 100 (yen)," said Joe Prendergast, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Credit Suisse First Boston in London. \par \par \uc2  "But chances of an active yen-depreciation policy from the G7 look very small in the context of a Japanese recovery and a widening U.S. deficit." \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 105.10/15 yen at 1155 GMT, nearly two yen above a 3-1/2 year low set in mid-September but still almost 15 percent below mid-July peaks from which its recent declines accelerated. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had briefly jumped to around 106 yen overnight, in a knee-jerk reaction to the G7 statement referring to the recent yen strength, before the initial euphoria quickly faded. \par \par \uc2  "We shared Japan's concern about the potential impact of the yen's appreciation for the Japanese economy and the world economy," the statement said. \par \par \uc2  It also said Japan pledged to "implement stimulus measures until domestic demand-led growth is solidly in place and, in the context of their zero interest rate policy, to provide ample liquidity until deflationary concerns are dispelled." \par \par \uc2  MONETARY EASING A STICKING POINT \par \par \uc2  A further easing in the Bank of Japan's already loose monetary policy, which many analysts see as a prerequisite for concerted G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , continued to be a sticking point after the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's refusal last week to have its monetary policy dictated by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami tried to clarify the BOJ's position at the weekend, saying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates were an important factor and that the bank would respond appropriately and in a timely way to developments in the economy and markets. \par \par \uc2  However, he added that the bank's policy had not changed since last week's policy council meeting. \par \par \uc2  Neil MacKinnon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Merrill Lynch in London, said the market was watching how committed the BOJ was to providing monetary policy backing to \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies. \par \par \uc2  "While the market is certainly wary of pushing dollar/yen lower at the moment, I think it would want to see a concrete evidence of a change in Japanese monetary policy," he observed. "Otherwise, there will be every incentive to resume the yen buying we saw previously." \par \par \uc2  David Coleman, chief economist at CIBC World Markets in London, agreed that Hayami comments were keeping the dollar underpinned for now, but probably not for very long. \par \par \uc2  "We think it is (holding) for the time being in the sense that Hayami's comments have just introduced an element of uncertainty and perhaps a little bit of confusion," he said. \par \par \uc2  "It depends partly on what form the Bank of Japan's actions took - whether it was just marginal increase in liquidity or whether they show that they were determined to force the yen lower with big increases in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and things like that," he said. \par \par \uc2  "But it's not our expectation that the trend is going to change dramatically at the moment." ((London Capital Markets +44-171-542-6721, shinichi.kishima@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv9r032ef\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
