\par\par \b \uc2  G7 Partners Still Seek Japanese Policy Response \b0\par\par\uc2  By Damian Milverton \par \uc2 797 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 1999\par 19:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--This weekend's Group of Seven meeting may well represent a hollow victory for the Japanese delegation. \par \par \uc2  Looking for help in combatting a resurgent yen, they were rewarded with a G7 communique declaring that the other nations "shared Japan's concern about the potential impact of the yen's appreciation." \par \par \uc2  However, that's as far as Japan's partners would go. Instead of a warning that steps would be taken to guard against any further damaging yen strength, there was instead an emphasis on Japan's policy response. \par \par \uc2  Recovery and private demand remain weak despite a resumption of output growth, the G7 noted, and prospects remain uncertain. \par \par \uc2  "In these circumstances, and in view of the yen's appreciation, the Japanese authorities reiterated their intention to implement stimulus measures until domestic demand-led growth is solidly in place and, in the context of their zero-interest-rate policy, to provide ample liquidity until deflationary concerns are dispelled." \par \par \uc2  In one of the longest communiques to follow a regular meeting of G7 finance ministers and central bankers, this paragraph dominates. \par \par \uc2  But what does it mean? \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers told reporters to pay particular attention to the statements of the Japanese delegation, led by Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa and Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ "is prepared to use the flexibility it has in the context of the zero interest rate policy where ample liquidity is provided to respond appropriately and timely to developments in the economy as well as in the financial markets, including the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Hayami said, closely following the G7 script at a news conference following the meeting. \par \par \uc2  "This has been met with the understanding of other countries (present at the meeting)," he said. \par \par \uc2  Global financial markets had been under the impression in recent weeks that the Japanese policy-making process had been backfiring, with diverging policy goals at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  The overriding view was that the BoJ had been digging in its heels and resisting both domestic and international pressure to make its monetary policy even more accomodating so as to take upward pressure off the yen. The BoJ came under fire, for example, for having systematically sterilized the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  it undertook on the MoF's orders to push the yen down. \par \par \uc2  But some G7 delegates Saturday stressed that the Japanese policy motor is now running more sweetly, with both authorities pulling in the same direction. \par \par \uc2  French Finance Minister Dominique Strauss-Kahn acknowledged that there had been "misunderstandings" over the direction of Japanese policy, both inside Japan and between Japan and its G7 partners, but said these had now been dispelled. \par \par \uc2  The situation as regards Japan "is much better than it was 10 days ago," he said. \par \par \uc2  Another European delegate said assertions that the BoJ had stubbornly refused to conduct an unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not necessarily have been justified. "How do you know what the real liquidity needs of the Japanese economy have been?" he said, raising the possibility that, unseen to the market, the BoJ has in fact been adding liquidity to the domestic money market. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par              BOJ Plays A Discrete Game\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some of those officials said that Japan hinted that it may have more\par in mind than it is currently letting on.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But if that's the case, the BoJ is playing its cards close to its\par chest. Hayami's remarks Saturday didn't diverge from recent comments.\par But even if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  did have something new in mind, Hayami\par wouldn't likely reveal those plans.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Recent moves by the BoJ suggest that outside pressure isn't likely to\par meet much success in getting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to change its stance.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Last week the world was expecting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cave in to\par pressure to implement some form of quantitative easing measures to curb\par upward pressure on the yen. The dollar fell over two yen when the world\par found out it was wrong and the BoJ left policy unchanged.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As markets were still reeling from the news, the BoJ issued a stark\par statement asserting its independence from outside influence. This was a\par clear message not only to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  but also to G7\par countries that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't be pushed around.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At the same time, the G7 communique demonstrates that pressure on the\par BoJ to act won't dissipate, and in fact is likely to mount now that\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's partners have refrained from foreshadowing concerted\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to drive down the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Damian Milverton; 202-607-4371.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Arran Scott and David G. Pearson contributed to this story.)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 26-09-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1715GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1144 4220 62552 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9q07376\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
