\par\par \b \uc2  Tietmeyer warns on inflation, "bubble economies". \b0\par\par\uc2  By Janet Guttsman \par \uc2 479 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 1999\par 05:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON, Sept 25 (Reuters) - The former head of the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in farewell remarks to power brokers in Washington, said on Saturday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rarely worked and warned about "bubble economies" where high stock prices fuel massive spending and unsustainable growth. \par \par \uc2  Hans Tietmeyer, who left the German Bundesbank last month after 40 years in public office, named no country in his brief summary of the risks of financial bubbles. \par \par \uc2  But other experts have not hesitated to point the finger at the United States, where stock prices recently flirted with record highs before falling back some 10 percent. \par \par \uc2  "It should not be disregarded that bubbles in market segments may also pose macroeconomic risks, especially if the markets in question are such important ones as the equity markets in major economies," Tietmeyer told bankers, ministers and central bankers attending a farewell dinner in his honour at the Institute for International Finance. \par \par \uc2  "Of course it is mostly not until after the bubble that we know whether and to what extent it actually was a bubble." \par \par \uc2  Tietmeyer's hosts and invited guests praised the German banker as an elder statesman in international finance, and U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers said he missed Tietmeyer's frequent warnings on price stability at Saturday's meeting of the Group of Seven industrialised countries. \par \par \uc2  "There were times when it seemed we had forgotten for 10 minutes that price stability was essential - and then I remembered that Hans was not there," Summers said, apparently only half in jest. \par \par \uc2  Tietmeyer lived up to his reputation by warning the bankers they could not lower their guard against inflation, and he repeated a long-held view that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to change exchange rates rarely achieved its goal. \par \par \uc2  "If you have sustained overshooting of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , then ultimately \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not help," Tietmeyer said. "The only thing which helps is the adjustment of underlying policies." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when central banks sell a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drive its value lower on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, could occasionally have a signalling effect on financial markets, but it was no substitute for policy adjustment, he added. \par \par \uc2  The G7 finance ministers and central bankers, meeting without Tietmeyer for the first time in many sessions, issued a statement that expressed concern about the recent rise of the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  But they gave no indication they were ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drive the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower and said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed further action to stimulate its economy and cement a tentative recovery. \par \par \uc2  Tietmeyer also criticised the massive international rescue deals that marked the world financial crisis of recent years. \par \par \uc2  International lenders needed to take a catalytic role rather than stepping in with large bailouts, he said. "Solving a crisis with generous bailouts is only prone to lead to a larger bailout for the next and worse crisis," he said. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv9q0313k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscale