\par\par \b \uc2  JGBs retain gains by midday, eyes on G7 meeting. \b0\par\par\uc2 558 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 1999\par 05:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sep 24 (Reuters) - Japanese government bond (JGB) cash and futures prices held on to healthy early gains by midday in Tokyo on Friday, buoyed by a sharp slide in Tokyo share prices. \par \par \uc2  But activity was light and the upside was seen limited for the rest of the day, as operators were expected to avoid taking large positions ahead of a meeting of Group of Seven finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors to be held this weekend. \par \par \uc2  "People who built new longs are likely to square them in the afternoon, as they don't want to take risks ahead of the G7 meeting over the weekend," said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei stock average ended the morning session down 3.36 percent at 16,743.83 following a 205-point drop in the Dow Jones Industrial Average overnight and persistent yen strength. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei's tumble, which followed a similarly alarming drop on Wednesday, was seen by theb bond market as further dimming Japan's economic recovery prospects and ensuring that interest rates will remain at rock bottom for some time yet. \par \par \uc2  The key March 10-year JGB futures contract ended the morning session at 132.06 after hitting a high of 132.18, compared with Wednesday's close of 131.41. \par \par \uc2  The yield of the key 216th 10-year JGB stood at 1.735 percent, against 1.795 percent late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo markets were closed on Thursday for a national holiday. \par \par \uc2  Demand for cash JGBs was firm across the board, with traders seeing an eventual test of 1.700 percent in the 216th 10-year JGB yield. \par \par \uc2  One dealer said that further purchases of cash JGBs could lead the market to test resistance at around 132.50 in the March futures contract, close to a high of 132.65 marked on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The market, however, was nervous about further losses in Tokyo share prices, as it could increase political pressure for a bigger extra budget this fiscal year. \par \par \uc2  "Now that the possibility of monetary easing has disappeared almost completely, more losses in the stock market could lead to a larger extra budget," said a securities firm dealer. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei dived below the key 17,000 mark in early trade as market sentiment continued to be soured by the Bank of Japan's decision on Tuesday not to ease monetary policy, which dented hopes of joint U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the strong yen. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, Economic Planning Agency Minister Taichi Sakaiya said that Japan may be urged at Saturday's G7 meeting to undertake more fiscal spending to boost its economy. \par \par \uc2  But he said such calls were unlikely to change the government's stance on an extra budget. \par \par \uc2  Key June TIBOR-based three-month euroyen futures stood at 99.77, up from Wednesday's settlement at 99.72 which was set after a round of selling following Tuesday's BOJ decision. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the BOJ left the money market with an estimated fund surplus of 1.0 trillion yen through its 0020 GMT \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , unchanged from Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Key unsecured overnight call money was traded mainly at 0.02 percent, steady from Wednesday's weighted average. ((Ayumi Moriyama, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8550 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv9o035pw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
