\par\par \b \uc2  JGBs firm on Nikkei plunge, but cautious before G7. \b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 1999\par 04:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sep 24 (Reuters) - Japanese government bond (JGB) cash and futures prices posted strong gains in morning Tokyo trade on Friday, boosted by a sharp drop in Tokyo share prices. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei's three percent tumble in early trade, following a similarly big drop on Wednesday, was seen as further dimming Japan's economic recovery prospects and ensuring that interest rates will remain at rock bottom for some time yet. \par \par \uc2  Activity in the bond market was light, however, as traders braced for a meeting of Group of Seven finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors to be held in Washington this weekend. \par \par \uc2  The key March 10-year JGB futures contract was at 132.17, up sharply from 131.41 at Wednesday's close. Turnover was 7,161 lots. \par \par \uc2  The yield of the key 216th 10-year JGB stood at 1.735 percent, against 1.795 percent late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo markets were closed on Thursday for a national holiday. \par \par \uc2  "The market seems to have been bought as the Nikkei's drop is not showing signs of slowing even after it breached 17,000," said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei stock average dived below the key 17,000 mark in morning trade, as market sentiment continued to be soured by the Bank of Japan's decision on Tuesday not to ease monetary policy, which dented hopes of joint U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the strong yen. \par \par \uc2  Traders said medium-term cash JGBs saw stronger demand compared with the beginning of the week as players prepared for the end of the first half of fiscal 1999/2000 on September 30. \par \par \uc2  Key June TIBOR-based three-month euroyen futures stood at 99.78, up from Wednesday's settlement at 99.72 which came after a round of selling following Tuesday's BOJ decision. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the BOJ left the money market with an estimated fund surplus of 1.0 trillion yen through its 0020 GMT \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , unchanged from Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Key unsecured overnight call money was traded mainly at 0.02 percent, compared with Wednesday's weighted average of 0.02 percent. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8550 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv9o035kr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
