\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr/yen languishes as fears of joint action fade. \b0\par\par\uc2 533 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 1999\par 08:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Sept 23 (Reuters) - The dollar was hovering near its overnight lows against the yen by midday in Asia on Thursday, with the market increasingly confident Japan would not win wider backing in its efforts to curb the rising yen. \par \par \uc2  Trade was thinned by a holiday in Japan and reluctance to establish fresh positions ahead of a weekend meeting of the Group of Seven industrialised nations. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar gave up a brief early bounce towards the 104.40 yen area and stood at 103.82/89 by 0558 GMT, hovering near its overnight low of 103.70 yen following comments by Federal Reserve Bank of New York President William McDonough. \par \par \uc2  McDonough told reporters after a late speech in Evanston, Illinois, that the dollar's present level was not a problem for the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  "My principal concern is whether the exchange rate of the dollar is at a level which is likely to be good for the functioning of the American economy, and I believe the answer to that is yes," he said. \par \par \uc2  McDonough also said the "superb" performance of the U.S. economy was likely to continue and that the Fed had achieved price stability even with the unemployment rate at 30-year lows. \par \par \uc2  His comments reinforced a belief the U.S. would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try and halt the yen's rise, which is in danger of stifling Japan's fledgling recovery. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said a failure by the G7 to mention coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or warn the markets about an excessively strong yen would set the course for further yen gains. \par \par \uc2  "I see dollar/yen breaking through 100 as this gives speculators the green light," said Marshall Gittler, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk, Asia at Bank of America in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  "But because of that, the initial impetus to this rally will disappear," he said, noting that the yen's surge had been driven by foreign investments in Tokyo stocks. \par \par \uc2  "As the yen gets overvalued and the outlook for the Japanese economy worsens, these people will start selling their equities ... and repatriating the money, and that should cause the yen rally to be self-limiting," he added. \par \par \uc2  In the near term, chartists said a break of the 103.20 yen level would leave the dollar vulnerable, with no significant support ahead of the 100 level. \par \par \uc2  Euro/yen remained under pressure and was quoted at 108.37/72 against its early Asian levels of 108.92/9.00. \par \par \uc2  The euro was little changed against the dollar at $1.0444/49 against a New York close at $1.0438/45. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to leave rates steady at its meeting on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Chin Loo Thio, strategist at Paribas, said the euro's inability to sustain a rise despite upbeat economic data had left the market wary of political developments in Germany and budget debates within Europe. \par \par \uc2  German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder's Social Democrats have suffered a series of defeats in recent state elections. ((Sonali Desai, Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  desk (65) 870-3090; Fax (65) 870-3787; email: asia.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 @reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv9n03ax6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
