\par\par \b \uc2  Why BOJ cannot stop  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  sterilisation-Board's Ueda. \b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 1999\par 05:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 22 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) cannot adopt a policy of leaving \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilised, a member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Policy Board said in an article published on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Leaving the pool of yen left in the market after yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "not just ineffective, but harmful in terms of the credibility of the BOJ," Kazuo Ueda said in an opinion piece in the Asian Wall Street Journal. \par \par \uc2  He added, however: "It goes without saying that we are concerned with unstable movements in the yen." \par \par \uc2  Ueda defended the BOJ's decision to leave monetary policy unchanged at a regular board meeting on Tuesday, saying: "The decision reflects the BOJ's perception that it has been doing enough to fight possible deflationary pressures in the economy. \par \par \uc2  The board had been under pressure to ease policy to help curb the strength of the yen. \par \par \uc2  Ueda stressed that the BOJ will focus on the long-term perspective before addressing short-term issues. \par \par \uc2  He said the decision to maintain overnight interest rates at a virtual zero percent until deflationary concerns abate was "not just for the very short run, but for quite some time to come". \par \par \uc2  This policy decision, Ueda explained, has provided enough liquidity to the financial system without having to add more through unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Ueda also shot down the idea of inflation targeting, saying: "We believe that a move to such a policy framework would bring only minor benefits with possibly large costs." ((Tokyo newsroom (813) 3432-8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv9m03apq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
