\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar struggles as joint action prospects dented. \b0\par\par\uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 1999\par 09:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 22 (Reuters) - The dollar remained vulnerable against the yen on Wednesday as the prospect of joint U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  dimmed in the wake of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's adamant decision to keep monetary policy unchanged. \par \par \uc2  That speculation was also dented by a record high U.S. July trade deficit of $25.16 billion. Japan's trade surplus with the U.S. also jumped 24.3 percent in August from a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  But the market was cautious not to trade too actively before a Japanese national holiday on Thursday and a meeting of Group of Seven finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs over the weekend. \par \par \uc2  By 0635 GMT, the dollar was quoted at $104.67/77 yen, having been up to a high of 105.37 yen, compared with $104.75/85 yen in late New York on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The possibility of U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not realistic at this point given the even bigger U.S. trade deficit. It has made it politically difficult for the U.S. (to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," said a foreign bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ had been under heavy pressure to ease monetary policy ahead of the G7 meeting to help convince the United States to participate in concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Japanese politicians, meanwhile, kept up their verbal opposition to the strong yen and tried to keep up the pressure on the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  Chief Government Spokesman Hiromu Nonaka said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "should pay attention to the effects of current market movements on the Japanese economy." \par \par \uc2  Ichizo Ohara, senior member of the ruling Liberal Democratic Party and an informal adviser to Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi joined in, saying that the BOJ's decision on Tuesday did not match the government's policy and that he had conveyed this view to the prime minister. \par \par \uc2  "It just illustrates the confrontation between the government and the BOJ," a dealer at a Japanese city bank said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were unimpressed, however, and mostly shrugged off the comments. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said offers from U.S. fund operators were seen near and above 105 yen, while support was seen around 104.50 yen as the market was still worried over the possibility that a rebuked MOF may order more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It depends on the outcome of the G7, but we haven't completely ruled out the possibility of unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the summit," said another city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Senior Japanese Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda, trying to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation alive, said on Wednesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be discussed at the G7 meeting. \par \par \uc2  A sharp fall in Nikkei average was also limiting the follow-through yen-buying somewhat, dealers said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Nikkei 225 average\tab    closed at 17,325.76, down 3.39 percent or 607.03 points, its largest one-day point drop on a closing basis so far this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the market is waiting for news about a second extra budget as the absence of further monetary easing increases pressure on the government to come up with an even larger fiscal stimulus package.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere, the euro briefly firmed versus the dollar above $1.05, but by late trade stood at $1.0489/91, compared with $1.0495/00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against the yen, the euro was traded at 109.71/87 yen against around 110.01 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Mariko Hayashibara, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8478 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv9m03906\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
