\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan forex intervention \highlight\uc2  possible before G7-Suzuki. \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 1999\par 07:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 22 (Reuters) - There is a possibility of lone \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market before this weekend's meeting of the Group of Seven nations, a senior member of the Liberal Party, the junior partner in the ruling coalition, said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Yoshio Suzuki, deputy policy chief of the party, also told Reuters he still believed about four to five trillion yen in additional direct fiscal spending by the Japanese government would be appropriate in an extra budget for this fiscal year, despite the yen's recent rise. \par \par \uc2  Regarding the yen's rise after the Bank of Japan (BOJ) decided to leave its monetary policy unchanged on Tuesday, Suzuki said: "The dollar has rebounded a bit today. It's a good chance to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the yen begins to weaken." \par \par \uc2  "There is a possibility of lone \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the G7 meeting. It is possible for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to soothe speculative yen trade resulting from a misunderstanding (among market participants that the BOJ was going to ease credit further)," he added. \par \par \uc2  Asked if the government might be requested to expand the size of an extra budget for the fiscal year to next March in view of the yen's advance against the dollar, Suzuki said: "My view that four to five trillion yen in direct fiscal spending is appropriate has not been changed. "But politicians close to the Finance Ministry in the ruling coalition have said such an amount is too big. I would welcome it if such views would recede," he added. \par \par \uc2  The government has not decided the size and timing of any extra budget, but Economic Planning Agency Minister Taichi Sakaiya has called for additional fiscal spending of four to five trillion yen in such a budget. \par \par \uc2  Suzuki, a former Bank of Japan official, said he welcomed the fact that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had shown its independence and credibility by shrugging off intense pressure to loosen monetary policy on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  ((Yuko Yoshikawa, Tokyo Newsroom +81-3 3432 8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv9m037oc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
