\par\par \b \uc2  US MIT Krugman: Japan Should Boost Monetary Base -Yomiuri \b0\par\par\uc2 264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 1999\par 03:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Japan should expand the monetary base by adopting policies including "unsterilized" \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help turn the economy around, Paul Krugman, professor of economics at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology, said in an interview appearing in the Yomiuri Shimbun Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan can certainly expand the monetary base - it can always do that - and it would be very helpful for expectations to see it rising rapidly. It can do that in a variety of ways. I would certainly say that unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is appropriate now," Krugman said. \par \par \uc2  "Unsterilized" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would entail the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaving funds in the money market after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell yen. To date, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been carrying out conventional "sterilized" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to neutralize the effect of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on domestic money market interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Krugman added that he "would argue for purchasing long-term government debt instead of ordinary open-market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 " aimed at avoiding excessive day-to-day surpluses or shortages of funds in the interbank money market. \par \par \uc2  "I think that it is much more important for the Bank of Japan to send a clear signal that it is going to follow very aggressive expansion (of the monetary base) over a sustained period of time," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said an inflation target is appropriate, but there may be other ways to expand the monetary base. "Unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an effective tool," he said. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0144GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9l06xlt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
