\par\par \b \uc2  Hayami - Should stop rapid  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  moves by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 600 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 1999\par 13:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 21 (Reuters) - Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) Governor Masaru Hayami said on Tuesday that rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements should be stopped by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Referring to the recent rise in the yen, he told a news conference: "It is better to stop rapid movements by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets." \par \par \uc2  He added that the Finance Ministry was in charge of deciding on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and he thought \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would conduct "smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to cope with rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements. \par \par \uc2  Asked about views that the United States was demanding a credit easing by the BOJ as a condition for conducting joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, Hayami said he had not heard such demands from the United States. \par \par \uc2  He said he believed the U.S. thought the recent rise in the yen was Japan's problem. \par \par \uc2  He added that although the United States had an interest in Japan (economic conditions), he thought Japan had not received any specific request. \par \par \uc2  Hayami was speaking after the BOJ Policy Board voted to leave monetary policy unchanged but said it would provide more ample funds to the money market to keep the key overnight interest rate as low as possible. \par \par \uc2  This flexible use of market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  while keeping basic policy intact represented the weakest of expected measures that the board, under pressure for a further monetary easing to curb the yen's rise, could have taken. \par \par \uc2  At the briefing, Hayami was asked about the possibility of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He said it would be "rather difficult". \par \par \uc2  But he said there was a possibility that the Group of Seven nations might discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . G7 finance ministers and central bankers meet in Washington Saturday. \par \par \uc2  For example, he said, Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers had said a strong dollar was not contradictory to U.S. interests, but given the ballooning U.S. external deficit, Hayami said he wondered if a strong dollar had a positive impact on the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  Hayami also said he would keep in close contact with Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, adding that he did not think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Finance Ministry had different views on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On monetary policy, Hayami reiterated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would maintain its current easy monetary policy until deflationary fears abated, while expressing doubt about further quantitative easing. \par \par \uc2  "One cannot expect that providing additional funds would produce monetary easing effects," he said, adding that there were sufficient funds available in the money market through the BOJ's ample fund supply. \par \par \uc2  He added that a low interest rate policy and quantitative easing were two sides of the same coin, repeating that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would mainly use interest rates as a target for its monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  Asked if the BOJ is considering any new type of \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the current zero interest rate policy, Hayami said he asked the sections concerned to consider the possibility of a new money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He said the BOJ may use government Treasury bills and financing bills as a tool for a new \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but stopped short of providing further details. \par \par \uc2  "Instead of quantity (of fund supply), a new \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be aimed at penetrating the effect (of the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," Hayami said. \par \par \uc2  There is no time-table for introducing a new \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Hayami said, adding that it always takes time to set up the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's computer system to cope with new conditions. ((Yoko Nishikawa, Risa Maeda, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-3432-8570 tokyo.news room@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9l00cl4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
