\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Yen soars as BOJ stand dims talk of US help. \b0\par\par\uc2 400 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 1999\par 11:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 21 (Reuters) - The Japanese yen surged against the dollar and euro on Tuesday after the Bank of Japan kept its monetary policy unchanged, dimming the prospect the U.S. may join \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb yen strength. \par \par \uc2  The dollar dropped some 2.5 yen immediately after news that the latest policymaking meeting at the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  concluded without any new measures to further ease domestic credit conditions. \par \par \uc2  Markets had speculated that such steps would be a prerequisite for Japan to persuade the United States and other Group of Seven partners, due to meet on Saturday, to join their effort to curb the economically-damaging yen rise. \par \par \uc2  "It's the worst possible outcome for dollar/yen," said Stewart Newnham, senior strategist at State Street in London. \par \par \uc2  "Not only is the BOJ leaving their policy on sterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unchanged, but they are also making no effort to show a change in monetary policy," he said. "Effectively, it seems there is no credible official support for dollar/yen." \par \par \uc2  By 0826 GMT, the dollar had fallen as low as 104.42 yen from around 106.90/95 yen prior to the BOJ announcement. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the dollar had clawed back its most recent losses to notch up a one-week high of 108.16 yen on speculation that the BOJ might adopt measures to expand the local money supply. \par \par \uc2  Talk was that the BOJ could adopt either "unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", in which it refrains from draining excess liquidity in the money market which results from its yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or "quantitative easing", whereby it injects liquidity to achieve certain inflation targets. \par \par \uc2  "There was a lot of expectation built in for this meeting," said Yuji Tashiro, a dealer at Daiwa Europe Bank in London. "A lot of people had become long of dollars and they are now disappointed." \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar was poised to test last week's 3-1/2 year low at 103.17 yen, although damage could still be limited ahead of the G7 meeting. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan statement said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate was not a target of its monetary policy but said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shares the government's view that an excessive yen rise could damage the economy. \par \par \uc2  ((London Capital Markets +44 171 542 6762)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9l00ciw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
