\par\par \b \uc2  JGB futures end lower ahead of BOJ meeting outcome. \b0\par\par\uc2 744 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 1999\par 10:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 21 (Reuters) - Japanese government bond (JGB) futures closed lower in Tokyo on Tuesday, in wary trading ahead of the eagerly awaited outcome of a Bank of Japan (BOJ) policy board meeting. \par \par \uc2  Results of an auction of 1.4 trillion yen in 10-year government bonds carrying a 1.7 percent coupon were mostly within expectations. \par \par \uc2  The key March 10-year JGB futures contract edged slightly lower minutes before the futures market close at 0600 GMT, as players adjusted positions as the BOJ policy board meeting had yet to finish. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's nine-member policy board is widely believed to be considering adopting new monetary easing measures in an effort to weaken the yen. \par \par \uc2  The March futures contract closed down 0.40 at 132.04, after earlier hitting a low of 131.90. Turnover totalled 24,288 lots. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said its 1.7 percent 10-year JGB auction produced a lowest accepted price of 99.90 and an average accepted price of 99.95. The stop rate was 1.711 percent and the average yield 1.705 percent. \par \par \uc2  The results were much better that the previous 10-year JGB auction in August. The tail was 5 basis points on a price basis, compared with 15 basis points in the previous 10-year auction. On a yield basis, the tail was 0.6 basis points, compared with 1.8 basis points in the previous auction. \par \par \uc2  The bid-to-cover ratio was 1.81, compared with a poor 1.41 in the previous 10-year JGB auction. \par \par \uc2  "Overall the results were so-so. The (lowest) price was rather good, but the bid to cover ratio was below 2.0, which I think suggests that concerns of a rise in JGB yields going forward are still intact," saidKazuhiko Sano, chief strategist at Daiwa Securities SB Capital Markets. \par \par \uc2  The yield of the key 215th September 10-year JGB rose to 1.670 percent by 0645 GMT, up from 1.650 late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said investors may have been reluctant to bid actively at Tuesday's auction since the market was still waiting to hear whether the BOJ would ease credit. \par \par \uc2  "The auction results were maybe slightly better than initially thought, but some investors may have chosen to remain on the sidelines because of uncertainty about the outcome of the policy board meeting," said a city bank trader. \par \par \uc2  Expectations that the BOJ might announce a further easing of monetary policy provided support for short to medium-term bonds. \par \par \uc2  One option the market speculated that the BOJ policy board may be considering is increasing its JGB repurchase \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said the bond market opened weaker, primarily as a correction after JGBs were overbought on Monday on expectations of BOJ easing. \par \par \uc2  "I think the (JGB) market has already mostly factored in the possibility of a further monetary easing," Sano said. \par \par \uc2  After the BOJ's monetary policy decision, traders said the market's focus would shift to whether the United States would join \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in an effort to bolster the dollar against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Some investors believe such an agreement could be reached at a meeting next Saturday of Group of Seven finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said its auction of 1.3 trillion yen in three-month financing bills (FBs) on Tuesday produced a lowest price of 99.994, with 41.7706 percent of the bids accepted at that price. \par \par \uc2  The ministry also said it will raise its planned monthly offering of six-month Treasury bills and two-year JGBs in October by 100 billion yen each. \par \par \uc2  The moves will help offset the reduction in 10-year JGB issuance to 1.4 trillion yen from an originally planned 1.8 trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  The timing of the announcement was unexpected, but had little impact, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Tuesday, the BOJ left the money market with a fund surplus estimated at 1.0 trillion yen, unchanged from Monday. \par \par \uc2  The key unsecured overnight call money rate subsequently traded mainly around 0.02 and 0.03 percent, compared with Monday's weighted average of 0.03 percent. \par \par \uc2  Key June three-month TIBOR-based euroyen futures settled at 99.79, up from Monday's settlement of 99.78. ((Ayumi Moriyama, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-3432-8570 tokyo.news room@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9l00b7j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
