\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. stocks plunge, reel from one-two punch. \b0\par\par\uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 1999\par 22:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Sept 21 (Reuters) - Stocks reeled on Tuesday from the one-two punch of a record U.S. trade deficit and Japan's refusal to slow the yen's speedy rise against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Based on early and unofficial data, the Dow Jones industrial average ended down 225.43 points, or 2.08 percent, at 10,598.47. \par \par \uc2  The Nasdaq composite index tumbled 64.83 points, or 2.25 percent, at 2,821.32, a day after closing within just one point of its Sept. 10 record close of 2,887.06. \par \par \uc2  In the broader market, declining issues swamped advances by a wide 3-to-1 margin on moderate volume of 788 million shares on the New York Stock Exchange. \par \par \uc2  The market was dogged by news that the U.S. trade deficit widened to a record $25.18 billion in July, surpassing June's record of $24.60 billion. Economists polled by Reuters had expected the trade gap to shrink slightly to $23.8 billion. \par \par \uc2  Overnight, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, a move that triggered a drop in the dollar against the yen, pushing it down to 104.8 yen from 106.2 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also made only a token move to pump more money into its economy, bucking international pressures to lower interest rates and take the upward pressure from the yen, which threatens to cut into its exports. \par \par \uc2  "In short, they completely punctured market hopes for easier money in Japan," Jose Rasco, of Hoenig & Co., said in a note to investors. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the dollar hit a three-and-a-half-year low of 103.1 against the yen, as Japan's economic recovery showed promise. \par \par \uc2  The 30-year U.S. Treasury bond was down 8/32 with the yield rising to 6.09 percent from 6.07 percent on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, gold jumped $6.00 to $261.80 an ounce on the New York market, buoyed by the dollar's weakness and solid demand for the precious metal at an auction by the Bank of England of a portion of its gold reserves. \par \par \uc2  Gold mining stocks rallied, with Newmont Mining Corp. up 1-15/16 to 21-13/16 and Barrick Gold up 1-1/8 at 19-13/16. \par \par \uc2  Apple Computer Corp. was one of the session's weakest issues, falling 9-13/16 to 69-1/4 after warning that its earnings would fall short of expectations. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv9l038l5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
