\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar seen relapsing vs yen after BOJ stands pat. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tamawa Kadoya \par \uc2 620 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 1999\par 13:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 21 (Reuters) - The dollar will likely revisit recent three-and-a-half year lows against the yen following the Bank of Japan's (BOJ) surprise decision on Tuesday to hold its monetary policy steady, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Shrugging off intense pressure to loosen monetary policy and thereby pave the way for joint U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's recent surge, the BOJ said its Policy Board had voted to leave credit policy unchanged. \par \par \uc2  The yen, which had been edging lower against the dollar on expectations the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would ease its already super-loose policy, surged some 2.5 yen on the news to a high of 104.40. \par \par \uc2  It had stood at just below 107 per dollar before the BOJ announcement, which analysts and traders said had effectively killed any prospect of joint U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tame the strong yen. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar fell sharply after the BOJ's announcement, and the market will likely attempt to test its recent low of 103.20 yen," said Takehiro Sato, senior analyst at Sumitomo Bank. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell to 103.20 yen on September 15, its lowest level since December 1995. \par \par \uc2  Speculation that the BOJ would take additional easing steps has been building since Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa summoned BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami for a rare one-on-one meeting last Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The market consensus was that the BOJ had been persuaded to loosen policy further in return for U.S. agreement on joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen, whose recent strength may be threatening Japan's economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  "(The BOJ's decision) seems to dash expectations of U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Peter Morgan, senior economist at HSBC Securities. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the dollar's fall should be limited by caution in the market ahead of a meeting of finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors of Group of Seven (G7) nations on Saturday in Washington. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is not likely to go into a freefall ahead of the Group of Seven meeting," Sumitomo's Sato said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities were thought to have been eager to enlist Washington's help because the BOJ's own unilateral yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have become increasingly ineffective. "Japanese authorities will likely continue to conduct smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it is a waste of money to attempt to push up the dollar," a senior dealer at a U.S. bank said. \par \par \uc2  Smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  refer to \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at reducing volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets rather than reversing a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trend. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ took the unusual step of immediately releasing a statement after its meeting to explain its policy decision. The minutes of the meeting are usually released roughly a month after the meeting. \par \par \uc2  Specifically referring to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and monetary policy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it regards the yen's recent appreciation as rapid and believes it could negatively affect part of the economy such as corporate profits. \par \par \uc2  "These basic views on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and how the bank sees the yen's recent appreciation are shared with the Japanese government," the statement said. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  clearly stated that monetary policy would not target \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "Rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves should be stopped by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Hayami told a news conference after the meeting. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Miyazawa said it was understandable that the BOJ had different views on policy matters. \par \par \uc2  On \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Miyazawa said the MOF will take appropriate action on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  if movements are violent. \par \par \uc2  At 1117 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 104.59/64 yen. \par \par \uc2  ((Tamawa Kadoya, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8027 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv9l0374d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
