\par\par \b \uc2  SIMEX Nikkei futures end higher, eye BOJ policy. \b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 1999\par 09:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 20 (Reuters) - SIMEX Nikkei futures ended \par \par \uc2  higher on Monday, cheered by the yen's retreat from recent \par \par \uc2  highs.     Traders said the market was now awaiting results of \par \par \uc2  a Bank of Japan (BOJ) policy board meeting on Tuesday amid \par \par \uc2  speculation it might loosen monetary policy. \par \par \uc2      This theory comes alongside and idea that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has persuaded the BOJ to ease in order to strengthen \par \par \uc2  its hand in any negotiation with the Federal Reserve over joint \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yen - which has gained sharply against the dollar in \par \par \uc2  recent weeks and triggered some fears it could stifle Japan's \par \par \uc2  recovery - was hovering around the 107 per dollar levels by \par \par \uc2  Monday morning, compared to levels of around 103 per dollar \par \par \uc2  seen on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/yen should keep the market (Nikkei cash and \par \par \uc2  futures) up above 17,000 near-term though chart-wise, (futures) \par \par \uc2  are looking very bullish," a dealer at a local futures house \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2      The key December contract would nevertheless trade within a \par \par \uc2  band of between 17,000 and 18,000 points, she said. \par \par \uc2      A senior dealer from a local securities house said earlier \par \par \uc2  that market activity had been dominated by dollar \par \par \uc2  short-covering ahead of a meeting between Group of Seven (G-7) \par \par \uc2  finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  "We shouldn't see the market breaching psychological \par \par \uc2  resistance of about 18,000 before we get more news on possible \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S.," the first dealer from a \par \par \uc2  local futures house said. \par \par \uc2      SIMEX Taiwan futures edged higher, defying modest losses in \par \par \uc2  the cash market. \par \par \uc2      Taipei traders said trade had been quiet partly in \par \par \uc2  anticipation of a shortened trading week. \par \par \uc2      The island's financial markets will be closed on September \par \par \uc2  24 for the Chinese Mid-Autumn Festival holiday. \par \par \uc2   SIMEX NIKKEI 225 FUTURES Contract...... DEC9.......... MAR0 \par \par \uc2  Settlement....17565..........17555 \par \par \uc2  High..........17620..........0 Low...........17450..........0 \par \par \uc2  Prev Close....17260..........17250 Net \par \par \uc2  Change....305............0 Volume........15091..........0 SIMEX \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN MSCI FUTURES Contract...... SEP9.......... OCT9 \par \par \uc2  Settlement....353.2..........355.2 \par \par \uc2  High..........354.8..........356.4 \par \par \uc2  Low...........351.1..........353.2 Prev \par \par \uc2  Close....352.8..........354.7 Net \par \par \uc2  Change....0.4..............0.5 Volume........4964...........567 \par \par \uc2  SIMEX HK MSCI FUTURES Contract......Sep-09 Last..........9440 \par \par \uc2  High..........9632 Low...........9404 Prev Close....9522 Net \par \par \uc2  Change....-82 Volume........5 \par \par \uc2      ((Tamora Vidaillet (65) 870-3841;fax (65) 870-3787; email: \par \par \uc2  asia.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 @reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9k00hbu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex10