\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Treasuries steady in Tokyo despite strong dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 1999\par 08:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 20 (Reuters) - U.S. Treasuries were little changed in early afternoon Tokyo trade on Monday, with participants paying little attention to the momentum of the dollar's rebound against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The key 30-year Treasury bond was quoted at 100-31/32, yielding 6.05 percent, well below its recent peak of 6.13 percent seen last Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The key 30-year bond closed New York at 101 flat on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was rife with speculation that the Japanese authorities had gained tentative support of the United States for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but only on condition that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  undertake a substantive easing in monetary and fiscal policy. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese government is widely expected to unveil the size of a supplementary budget for the current fiscal year in the coming weeks, while the Bank of Japan's (BOJ) opposition to a quantitative credit easing is under the spotlight. \par \par \uc2  Some critics say if the BOJ resists extra credit easing steps, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be held responsible for the economy stalling due to an even higher yen. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ holds its regular Policy Board meeting on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  As of 0540 GMT, the dollar had risen to 107.86/93 yen from 107.05/15 yen in late New York on Friday and its 45-month low last week of around 103.25 yen. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury bond traders said, however, that whatever action the BOJ took on Tuesday to help puncture the ballooning yen seemed to have little to do with their market. \par \par \uc2  "A weaker dollar was blamed for selloffs in U.S. Treasuries in the past week. But that was rather because of weakening sentiment originally hurt by strong U.S. retail sales data," said a senior dealer at a Japanese brokerage house. \par \par \uc2  Since little key U.S. economic data is being released this week, range-bound trade is likely, with key bond yields moving around six percent, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Out of the limited U.S. data this week, the market focus will be on international trade data on Tuesday and the Federal Reserve's Beige Book report on U.S. economic activity on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  .. \par \par \uc2   for Key U.S. Treasury Rates \par \par \uc2   for USD GovPX-UST-Curve \par \par \uc2   for day's worldwide U.S. bond reports \par \par \uc2   for day's Tokyo U.S. bond reports. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9k00h4j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
