\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar starts week on firmer ground, eyes Japan. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Svea Herbst-Bayliss \par \uc2 601 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 1999\par 16:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Sept 20 (Reuters) - The dollar started the week on firmer ground, having jumped nearly three-quarters of a yen on speculation that Japan's partners may soon help tame the yen's strength if Tokyo says and does the right things. \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board is scheduled to meet on Tuesday and analysts said the group may finally be willing to ease already soft credit further to help dampen the yen's recent strength and entice Washington to help cap the yen's rise. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders began trimming long yen positions late last week, anticipating "the Group of Seven may agree on some sort of coordinated action" in the next week, said Sanwa Bank senior trader Jeffrey Yu, explaining overnight moves. \par \par \uc2  After a week of posting ever bigger losses, the dollar reversed direction and started the U.S. session around 107.75/85, up from Friday's 107.05/15 closing level and more than four yen above last week's 3-1/2 year lows. Later in the morning, it eased to 106.83/6.92. \par \par \uc2  The euro also lost some ground, slipping to $1.0396/03 from $1.0409/16 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Yen trading continues to captivate the market's attention. But with few dealers willing to stake out new positions before Tuesday's meeting, and many out of the market altogether for the Jewish Yom Kippur holy day, traders said the action will be thin. \par \par \uc2  "Today may be a non-event with the dollar enjoying little upside potential because it bounced sharply last week," said Republic National Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager Rick Gomes. \par \par \uc2  Dollar gains may be capped near 108.25 yen while losses should be contained near 106.50 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, dealers contemplated how the Bank of Japan may pump fresh liquidity into the system at a time when short-term interest rates are already around zero and the official discount rate remains at a record low 0.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Some said the Bank of Japan may agree to Finance Ministry requests to stop sterilising future \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This would mean that the bank would leave the yen it sells in the market rather than withdrawing them in daily money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers however had no firm view on how the United States and European nations may respond to Japan's moves. \par \par \uc2  Some said signs of good will by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could prompt the United States to participate in an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while others said the Group of Seven may only agree to make a stronger statement at their weekend meeting. \par \par \uc2  Finance Ministers and central bankers from Japan, the United States, Germany, Canada, France, Italy, and Britain are scheduled to meet in Washington and may discuss the yen. \par \par \uc2  In the meantime, dealers said Tuesday may also be a key day for euro trading, when a key German research institute releases its Ifo business confidence data. Analysts polled by Reuters predicted on average a rise to 94.4 from 93.6 in July. \par \par \uc2  "The Ifo data won't answer the question on German growth, but it could offer fresh hints that are important," Gomes said. \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the dollar also rose against the Swiss franc, inching to 1.5430/40 from 1,5405/15 and the British pound slipped to $1.6215/25 from $1.6233/43. The dollar rose against the Canadian dollar to C$1.4745/55 from C$1.4703/13 while the Australian dollar slipped to $0.6434/39 from $0.6461/66. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9k00bgq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
