\par\par \b \uc2  Mizoguchi/Kuroda -2: Kuroda Met Tsy's Geithner Late Thu \b0\par\par\uc2 218 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 1999\par 07:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Zembei Mizoguchi, head of the international bureau at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Friday he hasn't talked with Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda since Kuroda began his visit to Washington for talks with U.S. officials. \par \par \uc2  "I haven't been in contact with Kuroda since he arrived in Washington," Mizoguchi told reporters at the finance ministry. \par \par \uc2  When asked if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was asking the U.S. to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in coordination with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to weaken the yen, Mizoguchi said, "I can't comment." \par \par \uc2  Kuroda met with U.S. Undersecretary of the Treasury for International Affairs Timothy Geithner for about 30 minutes starting around 2200 GMT Thursday (6 p.m. EDT), but he declined to answer questions from reporters as he entered the Treasury and didn't disclose the details of his discussion with Geithner after the meeting. \par \par \uc2  The Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported Friday evening that Japan and the U.S. are close to an agreement on joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The report, which didn't cite sources, also says the Bank of Japan is likely to promise the Group of Seven nations that it will take quantitative monetary easing measures. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0515GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9h06tu6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\pic