\par\par \b \uc2  US/Quantitative Easing/Kyodo -3: Yen To Be Big G7 Topic \b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 1999\par 05:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The U.S. government has told \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  that in exchange for conducting coordinated yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it will ask \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to come up with a series of policy measures, including quantitative monetary easing, Kyodo reported. \par \par \uc2  U.S. monetary authorities are asking Japan to ease monetary conditions further by leaving yen sold during \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilized in the money market, Kyodo quoted an "international financial source" as saying. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. feels that by sterilizing the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds - or draining the yen funds after they settle in the market - Japan is putting a cap on the supply of yen and triggering a strengthening in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Kyodo quoted the source as saying. \par \par \uc2  The source said that financial deputies of the Group of Seven leading industrialized nations are scheduled to meet Friday and are expected to exchange opinions on cooperating over \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  The report also quoted a "G7 source" as saying that the strong yen will be one of the main items on the agenda for the Washington meeting of the G7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors later this month. \par \par \uc2  The Kyodo report originated out of Washington. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0300GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9h06tmp\par }\page