\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo-2:NY BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Would Be More Effective \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 1999\par 02:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dealers say that if other G7 nations were to agree to assist in Japan's efforts to keep the yen in check, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would probably first have to consent to perform unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That prospect looks unlikely for now, however, as Hayami flatly denied the possibility after his meeting with Miyazawa Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, on Friday, the BOJ sterilized Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as expected. \par \par \uc2  Outside \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Haruhiko Kuroda, the vice finance minister for international affairs, met with U.S. Undersecretary of the Treasury Timothy Geithner a few hours ago, but declined to comment on the 30-minute meeting. \par \par \uc2  "Without the help of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the BOJ will have to think more about timing," said a Japanese city bank dealer. "If they don't do it right, it'll in fact lead to more dollar selling." \par \par \uc2  The dealer said that even single-handed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have a bigger impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if it were conducted during New York trading rather than in Asian time. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was trading at Y108.92, unchanged from its level in New York late Thursday. The euro was quoted late in Tokyo Thursday at Y109.18. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6252, up from $1.6240 in New York late Thursday after gains on recent bullish comments from Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown about the U.K. economy. Sterling was at $1.6156 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is seen trading between Y103.50-Y105.50 for the rest of the Asian day. \par \par \uc2  By Chang-Ran Kim; 813-5255-2933; chang-ran.kim@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0059GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9h06tfr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
