\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Mizoguchi/BOJ-2: Asked About IMF Official's Remarks \b0\par\par\uc2 206 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 1999\par 02:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Zembei Mizoguchi, head of the international bureau at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Friday that he can't comment on the issue of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sterilization of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Asked about overnight remarks by an unnamed senior International Monetary Fund official noting that there have been calls for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  not to sterilize its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mizoguchi said: "It's not our position to comment on whether the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  should sterilize \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds." The BOJ has historically kept to a policy of always sterilizing \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Asked if Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda will ask the U.S. for a help in curbing yen appreciation, Mizoguchi said, "I can't comment on if Kuroda will ask for that. The U.S. and Japan are always in close contact on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  matters." Kuroda is in Washington late Thursday and early Friday for meetings with U.S. officials. \par \par \uc2  Regarding the recent moves of the dollar/yen, Mizoguchi said, "As usual, we are closely watching \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves." \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi spoke to reporters upon arriving at the ministry. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-09-99 \par \par 