\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar eases as Kuroda and Geithner keep silent. \b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 1999\par 03:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO Sept 17 (Reuters) - The dollar eased against the yen early on Friday morning due to a lack of dollar-supportive comments from a meeting between senior Japanese and U.S. financial officials Haruhiko Kuroda and Timothy Geithner, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The greenback was also blocked by offers above 105 yen by foreign operators and Japanese exporters. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said they were reluctant to sell the dollar aggressively as wariness of the potential for joint Japan-U.S. action was mounting ahead of a G7 meeting next week. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 104.93/00 yen as of 0041 GMT against 105.05/15 yen in late New York on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was quoted at $1.0385/95 as of 0044 GMT against $1.0370/75 in New York. Haruhiko Kuroda, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, met Timothy Geithner, the U.S. Treasury's undersecretary for international affairs in Washington late on Thursday amid mounting speculation of the potential for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese and U.S. monetary authorities. \par \par \uc2  A city bank dealer said: "It's hard to tell if there actually will be any joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it will be a central market theme going into next week's G7 meeting." \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said on Friday he expects to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates at an upcoming meeting of Group of Seven nations or in a bilateral meeting with the United States later this month. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues will be discussed at the G7 meeting in Washington on September 25 or in a bilateral meeting with the United States, Miyazawa told reporters: "I think so." \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters in London thought it unlikely that the United States would join \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb rises in the yen. \par \par \uc2  Of 28 economists polled, 15 put the chances of U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming month at below 50 percent and eight above. The other five rated it at 50-50. Dealers said the dollar could also be supported by moves to square positions ahead of the weekend, which could be exaggerated due to worries about Hurricane Floyd which has caused widespread damage on the U.S. East Coast. \par \par \uc2  G7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors are to hold a meeting on the sidelines of IMF/World Bank meetings on September 25 in Washington. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 5473 3748 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9h00idm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
