\par\par \b \uc2  FACTBOX-Key issues in the talks over a strong yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 516 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 1999\par 07:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 17 (Reuters) - The following are the main issues under discussion as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  tries to deal with a relentlessly stronger yen: \par \par \uc2  JOINT \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  - The prime issue at stake is whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  can persuade the United States - and possibly Europe - to act jointly to halt the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  A concerted effort by Japan and other monetary authorities to sell yen in the global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market would be the most effective way to stem or even reverse its surge against the dollar and the euro. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current solitary \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market are seen ineffective in the face of overwhelming demand for Japan assets. \par \par \uc2  Japan sent its top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda to Washington to explore the possibility of joint action and lay the groundwork for discussions ahead of key Group of Seven meetings between finance ministers and central bankers in Washington around September 25. \par \par \uc2  BOJ STERILISATION - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is under increasing pressure to leave yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  "unsterilised," by leaving yen released into the money market untouched, effectively a way of increasing the supply of yen and ease monetary conditions. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ currently "sterilises" \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by removing from circulation the yen released into the market after it sells yen. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ has consistently rejected calls for it to leave \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilised, saying the issue is mainly one of monetary policy and that it would be fundamentally unsound and ineffective. \par \par \uc2  Proponents, however, say unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be a good psychological boost for the markets and display Japan's determination to tackle a stronger yen, something that could help persuade the U.S. into agreeing to cooperate with Japan. \par \par \uc2  MONETARY EASING THROUGH DEBT PURCHASES - Pressure is mounting on the BOJ to relax credit conditions further by increasing purchases of government bonds in the secondary market. \par \par \uc2  Further credit easing is expected to lead to a weakening of the yen due to the increased pool of money in the economy. \par \par \uc2  This is a drastic measure that many economists see as unavoidable, given the mounting political pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act if Japan's economy shows any sign of slipping again. \par \par \uc2  Japan has few other monetary policy options left, with its official discount rate at a rock-bottom 0.5 percent and short-term interest rates at a virtual zero. \par \par \uc2  FISCAL SPENDING - Japan may be asked by the United States to boost fiscal spending to get its economy firmly on a recovery track in exchange for cooperation on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  An increase in fiscal spending would intensify the need for the BOJ to fund it through dept purchases. \par \par \uc2  Japan's government is expected to compile a supplementary spending budget of around four trillion to five trillion yen ($37 billion to $47 billion) for the current fiscal year to the end of March. \par \par \uc2  After two consecutive quarters of positive growth in the first half of this year, however, the government has indicated that it may pare back its spending plans. ((Reed Stevenson (813) 3432-8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9h00fld\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
