\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Will Ask G7 Partners To Help Curtail Yen Rise, Report Says \b0\par\par\uc2 284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1999\par 06:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Japan is preparing to press the U.S. and its other partners in the Group of Seven nations to agree to coordinated action to curb any further strengthening of the yen, the Financial Times reported in its overseas edition Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Amid concern that the strong yen could jeopardize the country's nascent recovery, Japanese officials hope G7 finance ministers will agree at their meeting later this month to issue a statement similar to the one that emerged from a 1995 gathering calling for an "orderly reversal" of the yen's movement, the newspaper reported. \par \par \uc2  The U.S., which has so far given no indication that it will back stronger verbal or direct market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is treading warily, according to the report. \par \par \uc2  But the Financial Times noted that the last time the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the request of the Japanese government, in June 1998, to strengthen the yen, Japan agreed to policy measures to stimulate its economy. The U.S. may call for similar action this time round, the report said. \par \par \uc2  Zembei Mizoguchi, head of the international bureau at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Thursday the recent sharp rise in the yen has been "too much" and that Japan will take appropriate measures to counter the move. \par \par \uc2  "I think the recent yen strengthening has been too sudden," Mizoguchi told reporters upon his arrival at the ministry, adding that Japanese authorities are watching \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets closely. \par \par \uc2  When asked whether the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, Mizoguchi said, "We will act appropriately in line with market moves." \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 1999 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020329dv9g03psg\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 17/10/1999\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brd